  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The combination – pass, run and finish",
  "description": "Two lines along one long side: A close to the goal with the balls and B further out. A passes to B, who stops the ball and passes back. B then runs backwards down to the lower cone, turns and heads for goal. A carries the ball around behind the goal and, at the post, passes to B coming in, then steps in as a defender. B shoots.\n\nThe drill uses half the court, so another drill can run on the other half. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the floor, and show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: time the run so you arrive in front of goal as the pass is played."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: look up at the post before you pass."
    }
  ],
